<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2014-tumor-11--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2014-tumor-11: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.32";
    dc:description "The proposed skew of butyrate-producing bacteria toward depolarized oncogene cells is a spatial prediction with chemical and histological readouts. Those maps were not deposited with the incidence results, and general butyrate–HDAC datasets from other species lack the embryo geometry. The distribution model needs new or newly released measurements.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Map butyrate-producing bacteria, surface charge or membrane voltage, local butyrate, histone acetylation, and cell-cycle state across hyperpolarized host tissue and depolarized oncogene cells. Skew of viable bacteria and butyrate toward the depolarized cells, with HDAC inhibition there, would support the spatial model.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Bacterial attachment and bacterial viability can respond differently to surface charge, so both need to be measured.", "No public spatial microbiome or butyrate map exists for these tadpoles.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.64"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.321"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2014-tumor-11--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2014-tumor-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.25";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
